 "capsule": "Founded around 1235 when Sundiata Keita of the Keita clan defeated the Sosso ruler Sumanguru at the Battle of Kirina, the Mali Empire (Manden Kurufaba) became the dominant trading power of the western Sudan, controlling gold, salt, and copper routes along the upper Niger from its capital Niani. Under Mansa Musa I (r. 1312-1337), whose 1324 pilgrimage to Mecca broadcast Mali's wealth across the Mediterranean world, the empire reached its greatest territorial and scholarly reach, with Timbuktu flourishing as a center of Islamic learning. Weakened by Songhai and Mossi incursions from the 15th century, Mali shrank to a reduced Keita heartland that splintered among the sons of Mansa Mahmud IV after his death around 1610; tradition holds the Bamana delivered the final blow by sacking the old capital Niani in 1670.",
